  "content": {
    "problemStatement": "Let's denote the length of the Longest Increasing Subsequence of the array BBB by LIS(B)\\mathbf{LIS}(B)LIS(B).\n\nFor a permutation AAA of integers from 111 to NNN we can define two arrays of integers PPP and SSS, both of length NNN: Pi=LIS(A[1:i])=LIS([A1,A2,…,Ai])P_i = \\mathbf{LIS}(A[1:i]) = \\mathbf{LIS}([A_1, A_2, \\ldots, A_i])Pi​=LIS(A[1:i])=LIS([A1​,A2​,…,Ai​]), Si=LIS(A[i:N])=LIS([Ai,Ai+1,…,AN])S_i = \\mathbf{LIS}(A[i:N]) = \\mathbf{LIS}([A_i, A_{i+1}, \\ldots, A_N])Si​=LIS(A[i:N])=LIS([Ai​,Ai+1​,…,AN​]).\n\nLet's call a pair of arrays (P,S)(P, S)(P,S)  viable\\mathit{viable}viable, if there exists a permutation AAA with these arrays as PPP and SSS.\n\nGiven array PPP of length NNN, calculate the number of arrays SSS such that (P,S)(P, S)(P,S) is viable, modulo 998 244 353998\\,244\\,353998244353.\n\n\nInput Format\n\n\nThe first line of input contains one integer NNN −-− the length of the array PPP.\n\n\n\n\nThe second line of input contains NNN integers P1,P2,…,PNP_1, P_2, \\ldots, P_NP1​,P2​,…,PN​.\n\n\n\n\n\nOutput Format\nPrint a single integer −-− the answer to the problem modulo 998 244 353998\\,244\\,353998244353.",
    "constraints": [
      "1≤N≤500 0001 \\le N \\le 500\\,0001≤N≤500000",
      "1≤Pi≤N1 \\le P_i \\le N1≤Pi​≤N."
    ],
